 - **Aviation:** NOAA Aviation Weather Center for METAR/TAF data; `@react-pdf/renderer` for pre-flight briefing PDFs; 66 ICAO airports mapped (`src/lib/icao-codes.ts`, name + WGS 84 coords checked against AWC station info; only stations AWC serves are listed — a retired or unlisted code is removed, and `syncAirports` deletes stale `weather.airports` docs), seeded into the DB-backed `weather.airports` collection (2dsphere-indexed) via `POST /api/db-init` → `syncAirports`. Nearest-station lookup is the Rust Worker's `GET https://weather-api.mukoko.com/v1/airports/nearest` (the compiled-in catalogue, `weather_core::aviation`); the location page's aviation card calls `GET /v1/aviation/nearest-metar?lat&lon` (`workers/aviation`) — the nearest airport within 150 km that has a METAR in the last 3 h (candidates from the catalogue, one batched AWC request, per-station KV cache) — and shows the server's explanation when none reports. **The seed is not the limit (fetch on demand, #302):** when the catalogue holds fewer than `count` airports in range, the Worker asks AWC `stationinfo?bbox=` (same keyless host) for the METAR stations around the point's 0.5° cell, validates them (four-letter ICAO, finite WGS 84 coords, `siteType` includes `METAR`) and keeps them in KV (`avn:disc:v1:…`, with the stations themselves: 7 days when it found stations, 6 h when the area has none; upstream failures are never cached). The radius is rounded up to a bucket (25/50/100/150/250/500 km, `discovery_radius`) for both the bbox and the cache key; discovery shares the aviation circuit breaker (an AWC 4xx never counts, only 5xx/transport/timeouts) and never fails the card. The Python per-IP and service-wide discovery budgets are gone with the Python: one AWC request per cell per week plus the public API's per-IP rate limit bound the load (a service-wide D1 budget is a follow-up if needed). The `weather.airports` collection and `syncAirports` are no longer read by the app. AWC JSON gotchas: `visib` is a string (`"6+"`), `obsTime` is epoch seconds, `altim` is hPa. `fetchNearestAirports` / `getNearestIcao` remain as the static haversine fallback for the planner and offline use. Flight-category (VFR/MVFR/IFR/LIFR) badge colors are centralized in `src/lib/flight-category-styles.ts` (`FLIGHT_CATEGORY_STYLES`, `getFlightCategoryClass()`), shared by `AviationWeather.tsx` (location page) and `AviationPlanner.tsx` (`/aviation`) so the safety-relevant color coding can't drift between the two
